# Hostile audit — outer-detour diameter-moment floor

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Reviewed:** target_c_outer_detour_diameter_moment_floor_2026-09-12.md  
**Disposition:** PASS at proof-only Type-II scope; C-II remains open.

## 1. Outer-walk lower bound

The diameter endpoints of conv(A_r) are attachment vertices and hence extreme
vertices of the attachment polygon. They occur on the outer face of the induced
harmonic graph. The closed occurrence-counted outer walk has two arcs between the
chosen endpoint occurrences. Each arc is a polygonal path joining points at distance
d_r, so its length is at least d_r. Thus L_r>=2d_r; bridges and repeated vertices
only add occurrences.

## 2. Algebraic cancellation

Starting from the exact identity

S_out=2(a-S_D)+2(e_BB-k)-2d_tile-2C_A-Q_loc,

use e_BB-C_A<=2d_tile to obtain

S_out <= 2a-2S_D-2k+2d_tile-Q_loc.

With a=q-2+2c_I-d_tile, this becomes

S_out <= 2(q-k)-2S_D+4c_I-4-Q_loc.

The signs of d_tile, C_A, and Q_loc are all favorable in this direction. No
identification of Q_loc with the full global Q is made; loaded-touching global faces
may remain outside Q_loc.

## 3. Asymptotic consequence

The lower bound S_out>=0, Q_loc>=0, and c_I=O(D^(2/3)) give
q-k>=S_D-o(D), hence liminf(q-k)/D >= liminf S_D/D. The endpoint consequence
is a high-t floor only; no standalone lower bound on the outer-walk detour delta is
claimed.

The arithmetic script checks the endpoint constants and a separate high-t
normalized point. It does not certify a contact complex or global optimality.

**Classification:** audited-working proof-only Type-II floor; no theorem-state
promotion; C-II remains open.
